WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.870 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  a peak hour panic in one of hong kong's  busiest districts dozens becoming  trapped in a well-known shopping centre  after a fire broke out during lunchtime  rush  there was thick smoke billowing out of  the world trade center in causeway bay  firefighters trying to reach dozens of  people stuck on a podium and the roof of  the 38th story skyscraper  hundreds of others becoming trapped  inside while fumes filled a dining area  eventually all 770 were rescued  our firemen  discovered a heavily smoked log the fire  scene was heavily smoke locked at time  of arrival  so  to a fireman we found it  it is  one of the reason may lead to the  distress to the occupants inside the  building  authorities say the fire started in the  meter room on a lower level of the  building  an investigation is underway into  exactly what caused the fire the manual  alarm and sprinkler systems had been  disabled on the first five floors  because of renovation works the fire  department said it was only alerted to  this after the fire had broken out  this all happened in a popular shopping  area in the run-up to the holidays some  of those who were trapped would have  been out with their colleagues for  christmas lunch it's caused plenty of  chaos and distress and there will be  many people demanding answers brit  clinic al jazeera hong kong

